WEBVTT

00:04.380 --> 00:08.040
So, why'd you visit at a time like this?

00:08.040 --> 00:11.030
I wanted to get a certificate showing that 
I'm a member of this association.

00:11.790 --> 00:13.860
I wish you'd hurry and become a merchant

00:13.860 --> 00:17.660
that can make others flinch at your name alone.

00:18.560 --> 00:19.830
Otherwise...

00:21.950 --> 00:23.080
You go!

00:22.260 --> 00:25.580
That girl will leave you at the drop of a hat.

00:23.080 --> 00:24.000
No, you go!

00:25.580 --> 00:28.090
She's an investment of sorts.

00:28.090 --> 00:31.900
What's the point of investing in a town girl?

00:31.900 --> 00:34.370
I wouldn't invest if there 
wasn't something in it for me.

00:35.270 --> 00:36.760
Big words!

00:37.080 --> 00:41.310
That's right. Do any merchants 
want to go to Lamtra?

00:42.460 --> 00:44.940
If you're thinking about 
the shepherd girl, don't.

00:44.940 --> 00:45.640
Huh?

00:45.640 --> 00:49.760
There were a lot of people 
with the same idea as you.

00:49.760 --> 00:53.600
But no one wanted to hire 
that girl as a bodyguard.

00:53.600 --> 00:54.980
Do you know why?

00:57.530 --> 00:58.970
The Church?

01:00.100 --> 01:04.200
She's the only one able to wander around
 that area without getting hurt.

01:04.200 --> 01:08.460
There's no need for me to tell you 
how the Church feels about it, is there?

01:08.770 --> 01:14.420
If you get involved with her, you'll go through 
a complicated damn mess with the Church.

01:14.420 --> 01:20.640
Though, I know a lovely fairy 
like Nora is your type of girl.

01:24.420 --> 01:28.060
So, is this certificate addressed 
to a certain trading company?

01:28.060 --> 01:30.520
Yes, the Remerio Trading Company.

01:30.520 --> 01:32.270
Remerio, huh?

01:32.270 --> 01:33.540
Is there a problem?

01:33.540 --> 01:36.900
Yeah, well, you'll see when you get there.

01:39.050 --> 01:39.910
Here.

01:40.390 --> 01:41.910
Thank you very much.

01:43.250 --> 01:48.000
The Rowen Merchant Association is 
under the protection of Saint Lambardos.

01:48.300 --> 01:50.290
I wish you the best of luck.

01:50.290 --> 01:54.260
Once I finish up this deal, 
I'll buy you some good alcohol.

01:55.650 --> 01:56.550
Shoo. Shoo.

02:00.470 --> 02:04.690
Spice and Wolf

02:04.690 --> 02:05.810
Spice and Wolf

02:05.810 --> 02:11.150
Spice and Wolf

03:31.480 --> 03:36.320
<b>Episode 9
Sweet Honey and Bitter Armor</b>

03:35.020 --> 03:35.770
Let's go...

03:35.770 --> 03:36.550
Yeah...

03:38.220 --> 03:40.170
How cute.

03:40.170 --> 03:43.490
They said I was as pretty as a rose.

03:43.800 --> 03:45.620
Don't humor them too much.

03:45.620 --> 03:50.370
Craftsmen apprentices are like starving dogs. 
They'll end up snatching you away.

03:51.730 --> 03:54.250
If they do, will you come save me again?

03:54.250 --> 03:56.820
Yeah, I'll save you again.

03:56.820 --> 04:00.090
Well, in the end, 
I was the one doing the saving.

04:04.460 --> 04:07.300
I do not know what kind of return 
you are expecting,

04:07.300 --> 04:09.970
but I will have you invest in me for now.

04:09.970 --> 04:11.660
You overheard?

04:11.660 --> 04:14.770
My cute ears heard every word!

04:16.410 --> 04:19.860
It seems you have taken 
quite a liking to that shepherd.

04:20.780 --> 04:22.980
Was it her meager appearance?

04:22.980 --> 04:25.820
Or the fact that she has a hard life?

04:26.350 --> 04:29.700
I, on the other hand, am a mere investment...

04:29.700 --> 04:31.410
Hold on a second!

04:31.410 --> 04:34.080
The things Jacob says 
is his way of greeting people!

04:34.080 --> 04:35.240
It's not like...

04:35.240 --> 04:36.210
Not like what?

04:36.210 --> 04:40.300
I-It's true that I think Nora is a good girl,

04:40.300 --> 04:43.970
and I didn't dislike my conversations with her.

04:43.970 --> 04:50.350
But that doesn't mean that I like you 
any less or anything like that!

04:52.170 --> 04:55.230
I was just teasing you a bit...

04:55.230 --> 04:58.060
I did not think you would
respond so sincerely.

04:58.460 --> 05:01.190
That makes me so happy!

05:02.590 --> 05:03.540
However...

05:05.950 --> 05:08.100
Males are all the same.

05:08.100 --> 05:10.000
They say whatever they want.

05:10.000 --> 05:13.260
So, how about showing me instead?

05:13.690 --> 05:19.080
Knights leave their shields and swords in 
the hands of others to show their sincerity.

05:19.080 --> 05:24.170
Since you are a merchant, 
how will you show your sincerity?

05:26.410 --> 05:27.470
Fine...

05:30.150 --> 05:32.510
Those honey-pickled peaches...

05:33.600 --> 05:36.180
What will you buy for me?

05:36.180 --> 05:37.740
H-Hey!

05:37.740 --> 05:40.400
You know better than to do that!

05:40.810 --> 05:43.360
You told me to ask for it cutely.

05:43.360 --> 05:45.570
I told you to ask honestly!

05:45.570 --> 05:48.480
I didn't tell you to use underhanded tricks!

05:48.480 --> 05:51.410
But was I not cute?

05:52.870 --> 05:56.330
Though, you were cuter.

05:56.330 --> 05:57.140
Wha?!

06:00.950 --> 06:04.220
Hey, do not be so angry.

06:04.810 --> 06:07.580
Your words really did make me happy.

06:07.580 --> 06:10.390
Are you angry with me even so?

06:13.010 --> 06:14.220
Fine.

06:14.220 --> 06:15.570
I'm not angry.

06:15.570 --> 06:16.650
Are you happy now?

06:17.950 --> 06:19.520
It would not be good to get separated.

06:20.410 --> 06:22.730
May I hold your hand?

06:24.170 --> 06:26.990
Yeah. It'd be troublesome if we got separated.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.880
Um, Father!

06:44.610 --> 06:45.920
What is the matter?

06:45.920 --> 06:47.100
Um...

06:48.470 --> 06:51.340
I would like to take the sheep...

06:53.060 --> 06:57.220
to graze in a slightly safer area.

06:58.050 --> 07:00.020
You will be fine.

07:00.020 --> 07:01.130
Huh?

07:01.130 --> 07:05.480
God has graced you with the power 
to keep wolves at bay.

07:05.480 --> 07:08.110
Do you not trust in Him?

07:09.900 --> 07:14.410
Your work was also given to you by Him.

07:14.410 --> 07:16.490
Please continue to work hard.

07:18.500 --> 07:20.870
Y-Yes...

07:25.590 --> 07:27.380
You seem to be in a good mood.

07:28.220 --> 07:32.300
Any merchant would be excited 
when there are profits on the horizon.

07:32.300 --> 07:38.140
However, the hunter is most vulnerable 
when it is captivated by its prey.

07:38.140 --> 07:41.690
Merchant trading isn't the same 
as hunting prey.

07:43.740 --> 07:46.290
Buying on credit, was it?

07:46.290 --> 07:49.280
That means you are currently 
in debt, are you not?

07:49.280 --> 07:53.360
If you know something will sell, 
shouldn't you buy it even if you go into debt?

07:53.720 --> 07:55.300
If I did the same thing with apples,

07:55.300 --> 07:57.760
someone would eat them 
until I fell into the red.

07:57.760 --> 07:58.660
Fool.

07:59.010 --> 08:02.980
Either way, being in debt 
does not suit my nature.

08:04.010 --> 08:06.340
Even though you're currently buried in debt?

08:06.340 --> 08:10.810
If you wish for me to pay you back, 
you should ensure my happiness.

08:11.850 --> 08:14.180
Sure, sure. I will work hard.

08:17.190 --> 08:22.140
We just need to sell the goods we purchased 
to the trading company here.

08:23.220 --> 08:24.740
There's nothing to worry about.

08:30.690 --> 08:32.850
It is lively everywhere you look.

08:34.910 --> 08:37.120
It's the busy season, after all.

08:40.480 --> 08:43.580
I do not smell any honey-pickled peaches.

08:43.580 --> 08:45.790
I told you it's a rare item.

08:54.420 --> 08:57.660
Does a monk manage this place?

08:57.660 --> 09:00.820
If so, we'd at least hear some praying.

09:04.740 --> 09:06.730
Though, the crunch of eating 
that pie is so loud,

09:06.730 --> 09:10.160
your amazing ears may have missed it.

09:10.160 --> 09:13.150
What skillful sarcasm.

09:15.060 --> 09:18.620
However, I can at least hear 
the sound of the people inside.

09:18.620 --> 09:20.530
There are people inside?

09:20.530 --> 09:21.580
Yes.

09:21.580 --> 09:24.580
However, the atmosphere seems quite unpleasant.

09:24.580 --> 09:27.620
Well, nothing will happen if I stand out here.

09:27.620 --> 09:30.040
I won't make any money 
if I don't sell the product.

09:30.040 --> 09:33.340
Just as I will not gain nourishment 
if I do not eat this meat pie.

09:34.210 --> 09:37.580
That was supposed to be for my nourishment.

09:37.580 --> 09:40.470
Oh? Did you wish to eat it?

09:41.610 --> 09:42.420
Here you go.

10:06.740 --> 10:11.250
It is not yet the day of rest. 
What is going on here?

10:11.250 --> 10:14.090
Well, it's just...

10:15.790 --> 10:17.960
Did you just arrive in town today?

10:17.960 --> 10:20.100
No, I arrived a few days ago.

10:20.100 --> 10:23.010
Well, I'm not in any particular rush.

10:23.010 --> 10:24.450
I will visit another day.

10:33.270 --> 10:34.440
Are you Mr. Lawrence?

10:37.090 --> 10:38.200
You must be.

10:38.770 --> 10:43.010
You were planning to sell armor that you 
bought from Latparron Trading, correct?

10:43.010 --> 10:44.140
How did you know that?

10:44.140 --> 10:46.620
The Latparron Trading Company 
came by yesterday evening

10:46.620 --> 10:50.830
to tell us your debt was transferred to us.

10:53.850 --> 10:55.380
What is going on?

10:55.720 --> 11:00.720
It seems you are unaware of the recent 
drastic drop of prices in armor.

11:00.720 --> 11:03.820
Now that the northern expedition 
has been canceled,

11:03.820 --> 11:06.770
armor has become practically worthless.

11:06.770 --> 11:08.140
In other words,

11:08.140 --> 11:13.360
your companion now owes 
our trading company a lot of money.

11:13.780 --> 11:17.230
To put it simply, he's gone bankrupt.

11:17.230 --> 11:18.570
What did you say?!

11:19.970 --> 11:21.660
I've been set up!

11:36.250 --> 11:39.800
We both live based on such arrangements.

11:39.800 --> 11:41.450
You understand, don't you?

11:41.450 --> 11:43.470
Of course, Mr. Remerio.

11:43.470 --> 11:45.050
I am also a merchant.

11:45.750 --> 11:49.570
Mr. Lawrence, you were loaned forty-seven 
and three-fourths Lumione coins

11:49.570 --> 11:54.750
with a payment deadline when making your 
purchase at the Latparron Trading Company.

11:55.420 --> 11:57.820
This is what we wish for you to pay.

11:57.820 --> 11:59.860
If not,

11:59.860 --> 12:04.860
we will ask the Rowen Merchant Association 
to assume the debt on your behalf.

12:04.860 --> 12:05.910
Yes.

12:07.080 --> 12:11.130
Well, the deadline is the day after tomorrow,

12:11.130 --> 12:13.170
so we can wait the full two days.

12:13.460 --> 12:18.180
What do you want to do with the armor you have?

12:18.180 --> 12:20.080
It won't be worth much 
no matter where you go...

12:20.080 --> 12:22.380
No, I'll be sure to sell it at a high price.

12:22.800 --> 12:24.630
We will settle the debt in two days.

12:24.630 --> 12:26.560
Is that acceptable?

12:26.560 --> 12:29.600
Yes, we'll be waiting for you.

12:34.070 --> 12:35.510
Sorry for making you wait.

12:39.260 --> 12:40.280
Let's go.

12:49.990 --> 12:54.920
S-So, what has happened?

12:58.570 --> 13:01.090
The goods in our carriage have become trash.

13:01.090 --> 13:02.230
I see.

13:04.420 --> 13:05.470
Will you run?

13:05.470 --> 13:09.850
No, the information network of merchants 
is practically the same as the eyes of God.

13:10.110 --> 13:11.300
No matter where we go,

13:11.300 --> 13:13.850
we'll be found immediately 
if we do any kind of business.

13:13.850 --> 13:16.980
I wouldn't be able to live 
as a merchant after that.

13:16.980 --> 13:22.440
However, everyone knows that an injured 
animal will be eaten to the bone.

13:22.860 --> 13:24.400
Will you let that happen?

13:24.400 --> 13:26.000
Of course not!

13:26.000 --> 13:28.320
I just need to make enough money 
in two days to pay the debt!

13:28.320 --> 13:30.370
It's possible to make a fresh start.

13:31.950 --> 13:36.460
I am the Wise Wolf Holo. I am sure 
to be of some help to you.

13:36.460 --> 13:40.420
Yeah, just saving on your food costs 
would help me out a lot!

13:40.420 --> 13:43.210
I told you I will earn what I eat.

13:43.210 --> 13:44.880
I'm kidding.

13:45.510 --> 13:48.800
Your expression has improved.

13:49.250 --> 13:53.810
If necessary, on my honor, 
I will make sure you escape.

13:53.810 --> 13:56.640
Even if I must use the power of this wheat.

13:56.960 --> 14:01.490
You promised me that you would 
take me to the northern forests.

14:01.490 --> 14:04.120
I cannot have you falter here.

14:04.120 --> 14:06.570
Yeah, I'll be sure to keep my promise.

14:06.980 --> 14:08.030
And...

14:10.140 --> 14:13.370
If it really comes to that, 
I might ask you to save me.

14:13.370 --> 14:14.940
Leave it to me.

14:16.650 --> 14:19.080
So, what will you do now?

14:19.080 --> 14:21.250
For now, I'm going back 
to the Rowen Merchant Association.

14:21.250 --> 14:25.450
Yes, your fellow countrymen 
may be of help to you.

14:25.450 --> 14:28.100
That's why you should wait at the inn...

14:28.880 --> 14:32.140
Do you see me as the type of wolf

14:32.140 --> 14:36.960
that can groom herself quietly in an inn 
while her traveling companion is in trouble?

14:36.960 --> 14:37.980
No, but...

14:37.980 --> 14:39.660
Do you?

14:40.230 --> 14:42.640
No, but that's not the issue here.

14:42.640 --> 14:44.400
Then, what is the issue?

14:44.400 --> 14:47.610
The merchant association 
is a merchant's hometown.

14:48.220 --> 14:51.050
You understand what it means 
to take a woman there, don't you?

14:51.050 --> 14:52.900
Just explain it to them.

14:52.900 --> 14:54.870
How am I supposed to explain?

14:55.240 --> 14:57.660
Just tell them that we are lovers!

15:01.940 --> 15:04.640
Fine, please come with me.

15:04.640 --> 15:05.980
Of course.

15:07.490 --> 15:11.140
I will tell them you are my business partner.

15:11.140 --> 15:13.210
Don't say anything unnecessary.

15:13.830 --> 15:14.670
Yes.

15:19.770 --> 15:22.770
So, what should I ask about first?

15:23.090 --> 15:29.030
First and foremost, 
who is this beautiful woman with you?

15:29.620 --> 15:32.570
Due to some dealings, 
we've become business partners.

15:33.670 --> 15:34.990
Business?

15:35.300 --> 15:38.010
At the Pazzio branch 
of the Milone Trading Company,

15:38.010 --> 15:44.300
she was able to sell the furs assessed at 
140 Trenni silver for 210 Trenni silver.

15:46.670 --> 15:50.380
I told you I'd never invest if there 
wasn't something in it for me.

15:52.070 --> 15:54.280
If you were husband and wife,

15:54.280 --> 15:58.810
I was thinking of convincing 
the two of you to get a divorce.

15:59.300 --> 16:03.060
But there are guys like you 
every once in a while.

16:03.400 --> 16:04.210
Huh?

16:04.210 --> 16:08.900
One day, they have an unimaginable beauty 
with them and seem to... get along.

16:09.210 --> 16:15.240
Yet, they never talk about the woman, 
and I never ask about them.

16:15.580 --> 16:21.250
Well, the scriptures say it isn't good 
to carelessly open a mysterious box.

16:21.610 --> 16:23.370
A wise decision.

16:27.830 --> 16:31.050
Now, let's get straight to the point.

16:32.210 --> 16:34.220
Let me get this right.

16:34.580 --> 16:37.850
You bought armor at Latparron Trading.

16:37.850 --> 16:42.400
You were loaned forty-seven and 
three-fourth Lumione coins in the process

16:42.400 --> 16:47.650
and that debt was transferred 
to Remerio Trading.

16:48.060 --> 16:49.530
Is that right?

16:51.790 --> 16:55.920
Even though it looks like Latparron 
Trading pulled the rug from under you,

16:55.920 --> 16:57.700
I won't show you any pity.

16:57.700 --> 17:01.540
You got greedy and made a mistake. Am I right?

17:01.890 --> 17:03.330
It's exactly as you say...

17:03.330 --> 17:07.770
Robbery. Sickness. Injury.

17:07.770 --> 17:10.410
The merchant association doesn't mind

17:10.410 --> 17:14.540
doing everything in their power to 
help you in those kinds of situations.

17:14.540 --> 17:17.540
But that's not the case here.

17:18.340 --> 17:23.390
In other words, you have to return 
what you owe yourself.

17:23.740 --> 17:24.500
Yes...

17:28.810 --> 17:33.280
Unfortunately, I can't play favorites with you.

17:33.280 --> 17:38.820
Rather, keeping a firm attitude is 
precisely the reason I am in this position.

17:38.820 --> 17:40.340
Of course.

17:40.340 --> 17:44.830
I would also be angry if you had 
treated someone differently from the others.

17:44.830 --> 17:49.370
On top of that, members in the association 
may not lend money to another member.

17:49.370 --> 17:53.500
Of course, the association itself 
can't lend you any either.

17:53.500 --> 17:56.050
It wouldn't be a good example for the others.

17:56.050 --> 17:57.220
I know.

17:57.220 --> 17:59.690
The deadline is two days from now.

17:59.690 --> 18:04.500
Remerio Trading is feeling the pressure after 
failing in their own investment in armor,

18:04.500 --> 18:06.890
so I'm sure they'll want 
to collect it as soon as possible.

18:07.340 --> 18:10.340
In other words, your failure
 will become public

18:10.340 --> 18:13.980
the day after tomorrow, 
and I'll have to detain you.

18:13.980 --> 18:16.780
Do you know what happens after that?

18:16.780 --> 18:22.330
If I don't prepare the forty-seven Lumione 
coins and pay them back in two days,

18:22.330 --> 18:24.420
I will not have a tomorrow.

18:24.420 --> 18:25.750
No.

18:26.450 --> 18:29.020
You <i>will</i> have a tomorrow.

18:29.020 --> 18:34.780
It'll just be dark, painful, and heavy.

18:35.780 --> 18:37.840
You'd be able to pay back forty-seven Lumione

18:37.840 --> 18:41.970
by rowing a long-distance boat for ten years.

18:41.970 --> 18:44.210
You could also dig holes in a mine.

18:44.680 --> 18:47.770
But to do so without injury or sickness...

18:48.700 --> 18:52.910
It's not that I want you to die.

18:52.910 --> 18:55.190
Please understand that.

18:55.190 --> 19:01.700
Sins must be punished. 
I'm just carrying out common practice.

19:03.290 --> 19:04.230
Yes...

19:05.990 --> 19:09.710
If there is something 
I can help you with, I will.

19:10.040 --> 19:13.960
I trust you, so I won't detain you immediately.

19:13.960 --> 19:16.470
Do whatever you can until then.

19:16.470 --> 19:18.340
Thank you very much for your consideration.

19:18.620 --> 19:21.390
Businesses always have surprising loopholes.

19:21.390 --> 19:24.350
Sometimes you can only see them 
when you're in a pinch.

19:24.350 --> 19:26.640
Go and fight until the very end.

19:29.370 --> 19:31.810
I'll make sure to pay back the money.

19:40.640 --> 19:42.920
What will you do now?

19:42.920 --> 19:45.740
I've gotten two days’ worth of freedom.

19:46.090 --> 19:48.950
There's something I'd like to try first.

19:50.130 --> 19:51.990
Paying a debt with another debt.

19:52.970 --> 19:55.750
Oh, it's been a while, Mr. Lawrence.

19:55.750 --> 19:58.300
Do you have some new ways to make money today?

19:58.300 --> 20:02.630
I'm embarrassed to ask, 
but I'd like to borrow some money.

20:02.630 --> 20:05.060
Oh, is that the case?

20:05.060 --> 20:09.970
I'm sorry to say that money 
has been pretty tight lately...

20:09.970 --> 20:10.930
I see.

20:11.260 --> 20:13.730
I'm sorry for asking so much.

20:19.840 --> 20:21.440
There are still others.

20:40.690 --> 20:42.050
How was it?

20:44.350 --> 20:45.640
There are others.

20:54.310 --> 20:55.850
Maybe over there...

21:16.220 --> 21:17.300
Shit.

21:26.460 --> 21:27.300
Here you go.

21:29.660 --> 21:30.430
Next.

21:34.660 --> 21:36.190
H-Hey...

21:37.100 --> 21:38.180
What is it?!

21:41.770 --> 21:45.190
I am sorry, I cannot walk 
as I like in this form.

21:47.110 --> 21:48.030
No.

21:48.610 --> 21:49.710
I'm sorry.

21:52.100 --> 21:53.330
Excuse me.

21:55.150 --> 21:58.970
Oh, it's been a while, Mr. Lawrence.

21:58.970 --> 21:59.880
It has been a while.

22:00.320 --> 22:02.640
I'm sorry for bothering you 
after the market has closed...

22:02.640 --> 22:04.760
I heard from others...

22:05.060 --> 22:08.050
You've been asking for loans 
all over the place.

22:08.050 --> 22:12.970
A very large loan at that. Was it because 
of the crash in the armor market?

22:12.970 --> 22:16.520
Yes, I lacked proper vision...

22:16.520 --> 22:20.940
Only God could predict
 a market collapse.

22:20.940 --> 22:24.530
It would be harsh to blame someone for that.

22:25.750 --> 22:28.700
I live according to His word

22:28.700 --> 22:33.130
and believe in showing others 
the same sincerity I was shown.

22:34.330 --> 22:38.460
I wanted to be of some help 
to you, Mr. Lawrence.

22:40.080 --> 22:43.090
However, you're walking
around with a woman

22:43.090 --> 22:46.370
while depending on the mercy 
of others for money?!

22:46.370 --> 22:48.610
How dare you mock others like this?!

22:57.430 --> 22:58.740
Hey.

23:06.630 --> 23:08.100
Are you all right?

23:08.100 --> 23:11.180
You face is so pale! Let us go to the inn...

23:12.780 --> 23:13.910
If it weren't for you!

23:20.750 --> 23:22.860
I-I'm sorry...

23:27.810 --> 23:29.630
I will return to the inn.

23:35.490 --> 23:36.380
Damn...

23:37.980 --> 23:38.890
Damn.

